Ms. Manners draws an analogy to the "etiquette" of courtroom speech
codes. Such codes are not "etiquette", they are "law". If the judge
doesn't like the way you speak and you refuse to change, he will throw
you in jail contempt.

In sum, I agree with everything Ms. Manners says up to the point were
she starts contradicting herself.

