I realize this post is several days old, but I'm new to this group and felt
compelled to reply.  A person's right to free expression extend only as far
as the point at which they begin to infringe on another person's rights.  For
example, if I stood outside your window all day with a bullhorn shouting 
"CARL IS AN IDIOT!  HE IS A DROOLING, INBRED MOUTH-BREATHER!" I would _not_
be exercising my right to free speech.  I would be harrassing you and you 
would not be attempting to quash my free self-expression if you called the
cops and had my ass tossed in jail for it.

The point is, free speech is absolutely _not_ a license to go around
howling any damn fool thing that comes into ones head.  There is an implicit
responsibility that comes along with it.  And before you flame me for being
a censorship-loving, totalitarian, fascist Pat Robertson fanatic, allow me
to say that I'm against most limits of free expression.....just not the ones
that are COMMON SENSE.

