: I think, be a good model for a access to disk space.

Being on the system administration side of the fence (not at sdsu though), 
there are valid reasons for the admin. to check user accounts.  One of 
the things we check for are large executables.  If a lot of users have a copy
of a game, we are wasting time and tape backing up N copies of the
same thing.  What we would do (depending on the binary) is notify
the users that we are placing that executable in a common area
and that they should delete there copy.  We also monitor for
unauthorized access, possible security holes (like a + in .rhosts), etc.

We do let the users know that we do these things and that having
an account on the system means you agree to the conditions.  If
you don't get an account.

