Message-ID: <2mfs18$a5j@eff.org>

[Revision 2, based more old soc.motss articles.]

Summary: The sys op of the adusa.com BBS has complained to at least
three academic institutions about private emaiiil and articles in
soc.motss critical of him.  The results so far:
         Cornell U. - staff member must add a disclaimer to her nontechnical
                      public postings.
         Columbia U. - Public posting privileges of an off-site user cut
                      because one of her articles contained 
                      "Fuck it" and "stop fucking up his private email"
         Hahnemann - Same user expelled from the computer system.

Timeline:

*   Strange articles from BBS user John Stanley (aka
    "inward.stroke@adusa.com") start appearing in soc.motss. (Mr.
    Stanley apparently thought that he was sending private email, when
    in fact he was posting publicly.)

*   Several soc.motss readers including Syliva post articles and send
    email criticizing Mr. Stanley for inappropriate postings. Sylvia
    is a computer user at Hahnemann (a private secular college in
    Philadelphia). She posts from Columbia U.

*   Via email and discussion, it is discovered that Mr. Stanley's
    mispostings were caused by technical problems, not his own
    intention. Mr. Stanley and Sylvia are now on good terms.

*   Sylvia posts an article soc.motss apologizing for judging
    Mr. Stanley too harshly and saying that he would be an asset to
    soc.motss.

*   Melinda Shore, a staff member at a Cornell U. advanced scientific
    computing center, posts a general note to soc.motss saying that an
    netiquette guide is available by request via email.

*   Mr. Stanley sends email to Ms. Shore asking for the guide.

*   Ms. Shore sends the guide via email and, recognizing that he is the
    person who had his private email posted publically, suggests via
    email that he should probably find a better-run site if he cares
    about the quality of service he receives.

*   Sylvia continues to converses via private email to Mr. Stanley.
    One letter includes recommendations on how to find a better place
    from which to connect to the Net.

*   Mr. Mealey (aka hung.+adusa.com & adonis.bbs@adusa.com), Mr.
    Stanley's sys op, quickly replies via email to the email sent to
    Mr. Stanley. He says that some individuals seem "to be more
    concerned in creating conflict than in resolving matters in a
    civilized and amicable manner."
    [See enclosure <encl1.2mfeit$77d@eff.org> for an excerpt.
    See enclosure <9403170709362428@adusa.com> an article by Mr. Mealey
    talking about how and why he reads email sent to his users.]
     
*   Sylvia replies to Mr. Mealey and posts her reply to soc.motss.
    This is the first email she has sent to Mr. Mealey. She replies
    that she is now on good terms with Mr. Stanley and praises Mr. Stanley:
        'Seeing as how he was burned on soc.motss, most people would
        just say "Fuck it."  He, instead, saw one source of conflict
        and immediately offered to help.'
     She adds:
        'As a conscienscious user, he is an asset to your BBS.
         Treat him with care and kindness, and stop fucking up his
         private email.'
    [See enclosure <2lnbci$5qa@castor.hahnemann.edu>]

*   Mr. Mealey responds to Sylvia's article by complaining to
    Hahnemann (Sylvia's college) and Columbia U. (the site from which
    Sylvia posts.) In an article to soc.motss, he writes:
        'I suggest Sylvia you think twice about continuing this thread.
         Read the last PVT E MAIL message. If you want to continue it,
         it will be done on the phone from the Presidents office. You
         decide.'
    [See enclosures <9403121944571479@adusa.com> & 
    <excerpt.2m25ep$nqu@sol.ctr.columbia.edu>]

*   Sylvia posts to soc.motss with details of Mr. Mealey's threat.
    Namely, she says that he says that "he was taking to a fax
    campaign to my organization's president, letting him know what a
    foul mouth I had."  [See enclosure <2lu7cs$cq4@sol.ctr.columbia.edu>
    for full article] She finds his concern amusing since until recently
    his userid has been "hung.+", apperently in reference to the size of
    his penis (which he earlier had braged about in soc.motss.)

*   Ms. Shore posts a follow up saying that Mr. Mealey's writing is
    "really funny." [See enclosure <2lvdsi$182@fitz.TC.Cornell.EDU>]

*   Mr. Mealey reads Ms. Shore article makes a formal complaint to
    Norm Scott, Cornell's Vice President for Research and Advanced
    Studies. The basis of his complaint apparently is that Ms. Shore's
    article "chastize[d]" and "demeaned" him. Also, he says her past
    articles directed to others were objectionable. He sends Ms. Shore
    email telling what he has done and why. Ms. Shore posts this to
    soc.motss. [See enclosure <2m25m3$isc@fitz.TC.Cornell.EDU>]

*   In general Cornell U. finds little merit in Mr. Mealey's complaints,
    but Norm Scott does find some of Ms. Shore language inappropriate
    for Cornell. Ms. Shore suggests putting a disclaimer on all her
    posts stating that she does not speak for the University. This is
    agreed. Ms. Shore posts a report on the meeting to soc.motss.
    [See enclosure <2mcpho$rsr@fitz.TC.Cornell.EDU>]

*   Sylvia is expelled from posting via Columbia U. She loses her
    computer account at Hahnemann.
    [See enclosure <2m594e$nbg@sol.ctr.columbia.edu>]

- Carl

